  "id": "attitude-strength",
  "term": "attitude strength",
  "definition": "Attitude strength is the degree to which an attitude functions as a strong or weak guide for behavior. A stronger attitude is more predictive of what a person does, whereas a weaker attitude is less behavior-guiding and may be more shaped by the person’s own behavior.",
